### 3. Review Checklist for Worker's Implementation

| Item | Criterion | Pass Condition | Fail Condition |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **C-1** | **Target OS Scoping** | Code and dependencies gated behind `#[cfg(target_os = "macos")]`. | Compiles on Linux/Windows or leaks macOS symbols into non-Apple builds. |
| **C-2** | **Event Return (Swallowing)** | Monitor returns `None` when `Cmd+W` is handled; returns `Some(event)` for all other keystrokes. | Returns `Some(event)` on `Cmd+W`, causing double-emission via NSMenu. |
| **C-3** | **Strict Modifier Matching** | `(flags & DeviceIndependentFlagsMask) == Command` (or explicit exclusion of Shift, Option, Control). | Matches `Cmd+Shift+W` (stealing Close Window) or `Cmd+Option+W`. |
| **C-4** | **Key Character/Code Check** | Matches key code `0x0D` (ANSI 'w') or `charactersIgnoringModifiers == "w"` (case-insensitive). | Matches other characters or breaks on non-US keyboard layouts. |
| **C-5** | **Caps Lock Immunity** | `Cmd+W` still triggers when CapsLock is ON. | CapsLock flag causes `Cmd+W` to be ignored. |
| **C-6** | **Single Registration** | Registered once in `app.setup()` (`src-tauri/src/lib.rs:136`). | Registered inside per-webview lifecycle commands (`src-tauri/src/ipc/browser.rs:9`). |
| **C-7** | **Non-blocking Dispatch** | Event dispatched via `window.emit("menu_close_tab", ())` or `app.emit(...)` without blocking locks. | Calls blocking synchronous operations or acquires locks inside AppKit callback. |
| **C-8** | **Event Identifier Parity** | Emits `"menu_close_tab"` matching `src-tauri/src/lib.rs:102` and `ui/src/lib/tauri.ts:255`. | Emits mismatched event string name. |

